{"id": "project-detection-protocol", "question": "What is the Detection binary format and the ESP32 polling code for the /detect server?", "expected": "Packed 17-byte struct: uint8_t classID (1B) + float confidence (4B) + float radius (4B) + float location_x (4B) + float location_y (4B), __attribute__((packed)). ESP32 polls GET http://192.168.1.4:8000/detect every 1000ms via HTTPClient, reads http.getStreamPtr() with http.getSize(), validates size > 0 and size % sizeof(Detection) == 0, mallocs, readBytes, casts to Detection*, loops Serial.printf 'Detection %d: classID=%d confidence=%.2f radius=%.4f location=(%.4f,%.4f)'. Handles incomplete reads, malloc failure, no valid detections, and HTTP GET failure codes.", "expectedSources": ["Project_Prompt"], "tags": ["answerable", "code", "protocol"]}
{"id": "project-system-brief", "question": "What WiFi credentials, server URL, and navigation/movement split are in the original project brief?", "expected": "WiFi SSID Airtel_neel_8040, password air25322; server GET http://192.168.1.4:8000/detect. System: ESP32-S3 plus YOLO via API for now; navigation is Planning (D* Lite) plus Reactive (YOLO-detection avoidance) instructing the Movement module; Movement has 2 IR odometers with interrupt counting; WiFi dashboard shows status plus live detections with override/RC mode; entire project in Arduino.", "expectedSources": ["Project_Prompt"], "tags": ["answerable", "setup"]}

// ---- postProcessing 567 & NIMS ----
{"id": "postproc-567-derivation", "question": "Where does the 567 candidate-boxes number come from for our 96x96 YOLOv5 model?", "expected": "Input 96x96 with 3 anchors per cell across 3 scales: stride 8 gives 96/8=12, 12x12x3=432 small boxes; stride 16 gives 96/16=6, 6x6x3=108 medium; stride 32 gives 96/32=3, 3x3x3=27 large. 432+108+27 = 567 raw predictions in the output tensor.", "expectedSources": ["postProcessing 567 & NIMS"], "tags": ["answerable", "math", "specific-number"]}
{"id": "postproc-nms-slow", "question": "Why is post-processing slow on the ESP32-S3, and what does it do with those 567 boxes?", "expected": "The S3 must loop over all 567 raw predictions, check scores, and run NMS down to the one true object — that per-box loop plus NMS on a microcontroller is the bottleneck. Presentation script: the grids sum to 567 predictions in the raw tensor, answering 'Where does 567 come from?' and 'Why is post-processing slow?'", "expectedSources": ["postProcessing 567 & NIMS"], "tags": ["answerable", "reasoning"]}

